.TH MAKE:FORM 1 "October 2026" "SPP CLI Manual" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
make:form \- Scaffold zero-code declarative YAML form definition or fluent PHP form class
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php make:form
.I <name>
[\fB\-\-app\fR=\fIappname\fR]
[\fB\-\-yaml\fR]
[\fB\-\-php\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B make:form
command provisions form definitions in SPP. By default or with \fB\-\-yaml\fR, it generates a zero-code declarative YAML definition in \fBetc/apps/<appname>/forms/<name>.yml\fR.
Declarative forms support standard inputs (text, email, password, number, tel, url, hidden, textarea, select, checkbox, radio, toggle, date, file, range, color),
enterprise controls (signature, otp, tags, rating, repeater, editor, code, autocomplete, grid),
zero-code validation (required, min, max, unique, regex, match, range, file extensions, remote),
reactive modifiers (col, depends_on, computed, help, placeholder),
honeypot bot defense, and dynamic workflow state transition bars.
Passing \fB\-\-php\fR scaffolds a programmatic PHP form class adhering to the fluent builder API.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I <name>
The name of the form to generate (e.g., contact, student_registration).
.TP
\fB\-\-app\fR=\fIappname\fR
The target application context (e.g., school, default).
.TP
\fB\-\-yaml\fR
Generate a declarative zero-code YAML form definition (default).
.TP
\fB\-\-php\fR
Generate a programmatic PHP builder class.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
.IP \(bu 2
Resolves application directory at \fBetc/apps/<appname>/forms/\fR (YAML) or \fBsrc/<appname>/forms/\fR (PHP).
.IP \(bu 2
Compiles declarative schema or PHP builder stub with turnkey configuration.
.IP \(bu 2
Emits file metadata to \fB__spp_file_props.yml\fR.
